Subject: [PATCH] EE thread (FPS round 6): a leaner checkpoint charge, the plain call in one test, jalr calls
 with the lean begin and end

The runtime's own cost per call and loop checkpoint was 13-19% of the saturated game thread at 240 (the three
dispatch functions, all three machines, Amazon and Deep Amazon at draw distance 4). Every change gives the same
cycles at the same checkpoints and runs the same guest code in the same order. Each has a switch to the round-5
way (an A/B):

ps2xRuntime (runtime/ee_scheduler.h, Kernel/EeScheduler.cpp) - PS2X_LEAN_CHECKPOINT=0: as before:
- EeScheduler::checkpointDue reads the cycle scale once (m_scaleNow: the override, else the default, kept by
  setCycleScale) and makes one compare of the clock against m_stopAtCycle - the earlier of the held cycles'
  hand-over and the fast end - before the two flags, instead of the held cycles' sum and compare and the fast
  end's compare. The held cycles are the clock less m_heldBase (the clock at the last hand-over), so nothing is
  added up beside the clock; accountCyclesInline hands them on when the clock reaches m_heldStopCycle. Reaching
  m_stopAtCycle goes to checkpointLeanSlow, which asks what checkpointDue asked, in its order (the hand-over
  when cycles were just added, the flags, the fast end and the deadline / time slice). m_stopAtCycle is worked
  out again wherever its parts change (flushHeldCycles, invalidateHeldCycles, refreshFastEnd, reset, loadState).

ps2xRuntime (ps2_runtime.cpp):
- dispatchGuestCall: the plain call first - the switches it looked at one by one (hot stats, PS2X_DIRECT_CALLS,
  PS2X_DISPATCH_LEAN, PS2X_DISPATCH_HISTORY) folded into one test made once (g_plainCalls). PS2X_LEAN_CALL=0:
  as before.
- dispatchGuestBranch: a call (jalr, and the decompiled functions' calls) takes the same lean begin and end as
  dispatchGuestCall - the target looked up as before (callTarget), its level kept, the common end in place,
  callEnd for the rest (the target as the call's entry, as enterCall's) - instead of enterCall. Only the dispatch
  history ring (read by the missing-function report) is left out, as the lean direct call does unless
  PS2X_DISPATCH_HISTORY=1. PS2X_LEAN_BRANCH=0: as before.
---
diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ee_scheduler.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ee_scheduler.h
index 9466ad0..bbb38b0 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ee_scheduler.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ee_scheduler.h
@@ -18,6 +18,10 @@
